    <string name="open_emergency_dialer">Open phone dialer</string>
    <string name="sms_confirmation_notice">You must send the message in your SMS app. Check the recipients and location first. Carrier charges may apply. Opening the composer does not confirm delivery.</string>
    <string name="sms_app_unavailable">No SMS app could be opened. Use your phone to contact someone you trust.</string>
    <string name="dialer_unavailable">No phone dialer could be opened on this device.</string>
    <string name="sos_permission_denied">Location permission is needed to start SOS tracking. You can still use the message and dialer actions.</string>
    <string name="continue_on_device">Continue on this device</string>
    <string name="local_mode_notice">Use local safety tools without an account. Cloud backup and incident reporting need a configured server. SMS messages may incur carrier charges.</string>
    <string name="on_device">On this device</string>
    <string name="close">Close</string>
    <string name="privacy_information">In local mode, contacts, profile details, location logs, and recorded videos stay in app-private storage, encrypted with Android Keystore keys. Map tiles and links may use external map services. Preparing an SMS passes the selected recipients and message to your messaging app; you choose whether to send it.\n\nWhen cloud mode is configured and you sign in with Google, the backend receives your Google profile, edited profile details, and incident location reports. Optional backups contain encrypted data and media, but the server also stores account and file metadata.\n\nDelete account and data in this screen removes server account data when signed in, then clears this installation. Uninstalling or clearing storage destroys access to device-bound encrypted backups. Copies exported to other apps or sent by SMS are controlled by those apps and recipients.</string>
    <string name="terms_information">Rakshyaa provides personal safety tools and is not an emergency dispatch service. It cannot guarantee protection, phone coverage, accurate location, or delivery of messages. SOS tracking does not automatically call anyone or send SMS. Review and send messages in your messaging app, and dial the appropriate local emergency number when needed. Carrier or network charges may apply. Use the app lawfully and obtain consent before sharing another person’s contact details.</string>
    <string name="support_information">For immediate danger, use the phone dialer to contact local emergency services.\n\nFor SMS, install a compatible messaging app, review the recipient list, and press Send there. If location is unavailable, enable device location and grant location permission.\n\nLocal mode needs no account or hosted server. Cloud functions require a separately configured backend. Encrypted backups cannot be restored after losing the original device keys. Export important evidence before uninstalling.\n\nThis build does not provide a staffed response service or a published support inbox.</string>
